---

Simple personal CLI tool for generating Odin projects from either a Basic
(hello world), Raylib, or Library template. C and Go hello-world projects are
also available with the Basic template. C also supports Raylib, using CMake
to download and build raylib 6.2 as a static library.
Both C templates use unity builds: main.c includes the project helper
implementations and is the only application source compiled.

You must have the following CLI tools installed:

 - go for "--lang go"
 - jj (Jujutsu VCS) for "--with-jj" flag
 - fj (Forgejo CLI) for "--create-repo" flag

To build the project, compile the Odin build script once, then run a target:

 > odin build tools/build.odin -file -out:build
 > ./build build
 > ./build run hello-odin

Other targets are `release`, `debug`, `bubbletext-font`, `install`, and `clean`.
The `install` target writes to `~/.local/bin`.

Usage example:

 > otempl some-game                             \
 >     --type raylib                            \
 >     --description "Description for the game" \
 >     --with-jj                                \
 >     --create-repo

 > otempl hello-c --lang c

 > otempl hello-go --lang go

 > otempl my-game --lang c --type raylib
 > cd my-game
 > cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
 > cmake --build build --parallel
 > cmake --build build --target run

The C Raylib template requires CMake 3.24+, a C17 compiler, a supported build
tool, and platform graphics development libraries. The first CMake configure
downloads a pinned, SHA-256 verified raylib source archive. See the generated
README for release builds and other build options.
